      "extract": "The quantum electrodynamics (QED) theory predicts the interaction between photons, wherein the collision of two real γ photons can produce the e+e−pair, known as the linear Breit- Wheeler (LBW) process. The LBW process is the second-order process in QED [1], and its validation in terrestrial laborato- ries requires an ultrahigh-brilliance γ-ray beam with a peak cross-section of ∼1.6 × 10−29 m2 [2]. To date, the only",
      "extractCut": true
    },
