          "term": "polarization",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "SIMULATION The LBW process’s polarized scattering amplitude, with arbitrary initial photon polarization and ﬁnal positron (elec- tron) spins, can generally be described through the photon and lepton density matrixes. Stokes parameters and mean spin vectors can be utilized to describe the arbitrary polarization states of the photon and e± in the cross section. To establish a connection between theoretical predictions",
