      "extract": "section In the calculation of the completely spin-dependent cross section of the LBW process, we use the Lorentz invariant density matrix to describe the arbitrary polarization. The Man- delstam invariants in the LBW process are deﬁned as s = (k1 + k2)2/m2 e = (p+ + p−)2/m2 e, (1a) t = (k1 −p+)2/m2 e = (p−−k2)2/m2 e, (1b) u = (k1 −p−)2/m2 e = (p+ −k2)2/m2 e, (1c) where me is the mass of electron, k1,2 the 4-momenta",
